  <Placemark>
   <name>Marine Weather Statement issued November 21 at 7:00AM EST by NWS Key West FL</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_minor</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>The areas affected include...
Gulf Waters from East Cape Sable to Chokoloskee 20 to 60 nm out and
beyond 5 fathoms...

At 659 AM EST, National Weather Service meteorologists detected a
cluster of strong thunderstorms, capable of producing wind gusts
near 30 knots. These thunderstorms were located along a line
extending from near T Tower to near P Tower, moving northeast at 25
knots.

Locations that will be affected include...
P Tower and T Tower.</Snippet>
